  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Question": "In right triangle \\(ABC\\), \\(\\angle C=90^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle A=30^\\circ\\), and \\(BC=4\\). Find \\(AC\\) and \\(AB\\). Select the correct pair.",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(AC=8,\\ AB=4\\sqrt{3}\\)",
    "B": "\\(AC=4\\sqrt{3},\\ AB=8\\sqrt{3}/3\\)",
    "C": "\\(AC=4\\sqrt{3},\\ AB=8\\)",
    "D": "\\(AC=4,\\ AB=8\\)"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The leg opposite the \\(30^\\circ\\) angle is half the hypotenuse, so \\(AB=2BC=8\\). Also, \\(AC=BC/\\tan 30^\\circ=4\\sqrt{3}\\).\n\nAlternative method 1: 30° property and Pythagorean theorem\n\nSince \\(BC\\) is opposite the \\(30^\\circ\\) angle in a right triangle, \\(AB=2BC=8\\). Once the hypotenuse is known, the Pythagorean theorem determines the other leg:\n\\[\nAC=\\sqrt{AB^2-BC^2}=\\sqrt{64-16}=4\\sqrt{3}.\n\\]\nThus \\(AC=4\\sqrt{3}\\) and \\(AB=8\\), which is choice C.",
